What went wrong: The model permits a delegation to be active without the delegator holding the delegated role at the time of delegation.
Root cause: Missing constraint—the model does not enforce "delegator must have the role at delegation time" in the DelegationConstraints fact.
Fix: Strengthen the DelegationConstraints fact to require that for any delegation d, in any state where d becomes active (i.e., is in s.activeDelegations), d.role must be in s.userRoles[d.from] in that state. This can be enforced by adding: 
  all d: Delegation, s: State | d in s.activeDelegations => d.role in s.userRoles[d.from]

