[LESSON]: Alloy 6 does not support set subtraction with comprehensions of arity > 1; set subtraction must use unary set expressions.
[LESSON]: In Alloy 6, helper functions returning sets (like directRoles and delegatedRoles) enable clear distinction between directly and via-delegation held roles.
[LESSON]: Alloy 6 requires all predicate and function parameters to have explicit type annotations and to be separated by commas.
[LESSON]: Alloy 6 requires that logical constraints for "constructively enabling" scenarios should not just remove forbidden patterns but also ensure allowed ones are not blocked by other facts.
