    - DelegationConstraints fact
- Suspect: The DelegatorPersistentRoleHolding fact, as currently written, requires that the delegator always holds the role in every state where the delegation is active. Combined with Emergency-mode delegation transitions and mutex logic, this may create impossible cycles (especially if delegator must always retain the role, even when the role is delegated away or when revocation occurs).
- Action:
