**[LESSON]: Alloy 6 does not support inline assignment in facts (e.g., s.userRoles[u] += r) → Must use set comprehension or relational expressions to define state fields.**

**[LESSON]: Cannot use temporal transitions (like "Next") to define field changes unless a constructive fact or predicate explicitly permits or constrains the change.**

**[LESSON]: Alloy 6 requires constructive initialization of fields and a constructive mechanism for field changes (e.g., direct role assignment transitions) to avoid deadlocks or underspecified behaviors.**
